  "findings": [
    "The local isotropic Newtonian constitutive law requires symmetric viscous stress eta*(grad u+grad u^T). For constant eta and div u=0, the transpose-gradient contribution has zero divergence, so both controls agree exactly in calibration.",
    "The capillary force -kappa*(Laplacian c)*grad c differs from mu*grad c only by an incompressibility pressure gradient, and has the correct virtual-work sign.",
    "The independent real streamfunction basis is exactly divergence-free with zero mean. Its Dxx and Dxy derivatives and weak dissipation matrix 4*integral eta*(Dxx_i Dxx_j+Dxy_i Dxy_j) match the stated Newtonian stress.",
    "The instantaneous, zero-inertia-before-composition-change preparation removes a hidden flow-history assumption. All current patterns stay within the stated composition amplitude bounds.",
    "Repeated calibration settings represent separate measurements with independent fixed instrumental noise, not extra constraints on the physical solution."
